# User Verification & Email Confirmation - Complete Design Spec

## 1. DATABASE SCHEMA (Prisma)

```prisma
// Enum for email verification status
enum EmailVerificationStatus {
  PENDING
  VERIFIED
  EXPIRED
}

// Enum for phone verification status
enum PhoneVerificationStatus {
  PENDING
  VERIFIED
  FAILED
  EXPIRED
}

// Enum for KYC document types
enum KycDocumentType {
  DRIVER_LICENSE
  PASSPORT
  NATIONAL_ID
  UTILITY_BILL
}

// Enum for KYC verification status
enum KycVerificationStatus {
  PENDING
  APPROVED
  REJECTED
  EXPIRED
}

// Enum for overall user verification status
enum UserVerificationStatus {
  UNVERIFIED       // No verifications completed
  EMAIL_VERIFIED   // Email verified only
  PHONE_VERIFIED   // Email + Phone verified
  FULLY_VERIFIED   // Email + Phone + KYC verified
}

// Extend User model with verification fields
model User {
  id                String   @id @default(cuid())
  fullName          String
  email             String   @unique
  passwordHash      String
  phoneNumber       String?
  avatar            String?
  bio               String?
  role              UserRole @default(BUYER)
  status            UserStatus @default(PENDING)

  // Verification fields (NEW)
  emailVerified     Boolean  @default(false)
  emailVerifiedAt   DateTime?
  phoneVerified     Boolean  @default(false)
  phoneVerifiedAt   DateTime?
  kycVerified       Boolean  @default(false)
  kycVerifiedAt     DateTime?
  verificationStatus UserVerificationStatus @default(UNVERIFIED)

  // Relations (NEW)
  emailVerifications  EmailVerification[]
  phoneVerifications  PhoneVerification[]
  kycDocuments        KycDocument[]

  // Existing relations
  properties        Property[]
  connections       Connection[] @relation("ConnectionBuyer")
  connectionsAsSeller Connection[] @relation("ConnectionSeller")
  messages          Message[]
  viewings          Viewing[]
  offers            Offer[]
  transactions      Transaction[] @relation("TransactionBuyer")
  transactionsAsSeller Transaction[] @relation("TransactionSeller")
  reviewsGiven      Review[] @relation("ReviewerRelation")
  reviewsReceived   Review[] @relation("RevieweeRelation")

  createdAt         DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt         DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([email])
  @@index([verificationStatus])
  @@index([emailVerified])
  @@index([status])
}

// Email verification model (NEW)
model EmailVerification {
  id                String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId            String
  user              User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  email             String   // The email being verified (may differ from user.email during signup)
  token             String   @unique // Hashed token
  tokenHash         String   @unique // For comparison
  status            EmailVerificationStatus @default(PENDING)

  expiresAt         DateTime
  verifiedAt        DateTime?

  createdAt         DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt         DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([userId])
  @@index([token])
  @@index([status])
  @@index([expiresAt])
}

// Phone verification model (NEW)
model PhoneVerification {
  id                String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId            String
  user              User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  phoneNumber       String
  verificationCode  String   // 6-digit code
  status            PhoneVerificationStatus @default(PENDING)

  attempts          Int      @default(0)
  maxAttempts       Int      @default(3)

  expiresAt         DateTime
  verifiedAt        DateTime?

  createdAt         DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt         DateTime @updatedAt

  @@unique([userId, phoneNumber, status]) // One active verification per phone
  @@index([userId])
  @@index([status])
  @@index([expiresAt])
}

// KYC document model (NEW)
model KycDocument {
  id                String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId            String
  user              User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  documentType      KycDocumentType
  documentUrl       String   // S3 path or URL
  fileSize          Int      // In bytes
  fileName          String
  mimeType          String   // e.g., "image/jpeg", "application/pdf"

  status            KycVerificationStatus @default(PENDING)
  rejectionReason   String?

  verifiedAt        DateTime?
  verifiedBy        String?  // Admin user ID who verified

  uploadedAt        DateTime @default(now())
  expiresAt         DateTime? // For documents that expire (e.g., driver's license)

  createdAt         DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt         DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([userId])
  @@index([status])
  @@index([documentType])
  @@index([uploadedAt])
}

// Verification audit log (NEW - for compliance)
model VerificationAuditLog {
  id                String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId            String

  action            String   // "EMAIL_VERIFIED", "PHONE_VERIFIED", "KYC_APPROVED", etc.
  details           String?  // JSON metadata
  ipAddress         String?
  userAgent         String?

  createdAt         DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([userId])
  @@index([action])
  @@index([createdAt])
}

// Extend Transaction model (if high-value gate needed)
// Add field to Transaction:
// kycRequiredForTransaction Boolean @default(false)
// verificationRequiredByDate DateTime? // Deadline for verification
```

---

## 2. API ENDPOINTS

### Email Verification Flow

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Purpose |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| POST | `/auth/email/send-verification` | Optional | Trigger email verification (send link) |
| POST | `/auth/email/verify` | None | Verify email with token from link |
| POST | `/auth/email/resend-verification` | User | Resend verification email |
| GET | `/auth/email/verification-status` | User | Check if email is verified |

**POST /auth/email/send-verification**
```json
Request:
{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}

Response 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Verification email sent",
  "expiresIn": 1800
}

Errors:
- 400: Invalid email format
- 409: Email already verified
- 429: Too many requests (rate limit)
```

**POST /auth/email/verify**
```json
Request:
{
  "token": "eyJhbGc..."
}

Response 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Email verified successfully",
  "user": {
    "id": "user123",
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "emailVerified": true,
    "verificationStatus": "EMAIL_VERIFIED"
  }
}

Errors:
- 400: Invalid or malformed token
- 401: Token expired
- 404: Token not found
- 409: Email already verified
```

**POST /auth/email/resend-verification**
```json
Request:
{}

Response 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Verification email resent",
  "expiresIn": 1800
}

Errors:
- 401: Not authenticated
- 409: Email already verified
- 429: Too many requests
```

---

### Phone Verification Flow

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Purpose |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| POST | `/auth/phone/send-code` | User | Send SMS verification code |
| POST | `/auth/phone/verify` | User | Verify phone with code |
| GET | `/auth/phone/verification-status` | User | Check phone verification status |

**POST /auth/phone/send-code**
```json
Request:
{
  "phoneNumber": "+12025551234"
}

Response 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Verification code sent via SMS",
  "expiresIn": 600,
  "maskedPhone": "+1202***1234"
}

Errors:
- 400: Invalid phone format
- 409: Phone already verified for this user
- 429: Too many code requests
- 503: SMS service unavailable
```

**POST /auth/phone/verify**
```json
Request:
{
  "code": "123456"
}

Response 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Phone verified successfully",
  "user": {
    "id": "user123",
    "phoneNumber": "+12025551234",
    "phoneVerified": true,
    "verificationStatus": "PHONE_VERIFIED"
  }
}

Errors:
- 400: Invalid code format
- 401: Invalid or expired code
- 429: Too many failed attempts (locked out)
```

---

### KYC Document Flow

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Purpose |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| POST | `/kyc/upload` | User | Upload KYC document |
| GET | `/kyc/status` | User | Get KYC verification status |
| DELETE | `/kyc/document/:documentId` | User | Delete uploaded document (if PENDING) |
| POST | `/kyc/resubmit` | User | Resubmit after rejection |
| GET | `/kyc/documents` | User | List all KYC documents for user |

**POST /kyc/upload**
```json
Request: multipart/form-data
{
  "document": <binary file>,
  "documentType": "DRIVER_LICENSE"
}

Response 201:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Document uploaded successfully",
  "document": {
    "id": "doc123",
    "documentType": "DRIVER_LICENSE",
    "status": "PENDING",
    "uploadedAt": "2026-07-05T14:30:00Z",
    "expiresAt": "2031-07-05T00:00:00Z"
  }
}

Errors:
- 400: Invalid document type or file size
- 403: User already has approved KYC
- 413: File too large (>10MB)
- 415: Invalid file type (must be image/PDF)
- 429: Too many uploads
```

**GET /kyc/status**
```json
Response 200:
{
  "userId": "user123",
  "kycVerified": false,
  "kycVerifiedAt": null,
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "doc123",
      "documentType": "DRIVER_LICENSE",
      "status": "PENDING",
      "uploadedAt": "2026-07-05T14:30:00Z",
      "rejectionReason": null
    }
  ],
  "canResubmit": false
}
```

**DELETE /kyc/document/:documentId**
```json
Response 204: No Content

Errors:
- 403: Cannot delete non-PENDING document
- 404: Document not found
```

**POST /kyc/resubmit**
```json
Request: multipart/form-data
{
  "document": <binary file>,
  "documentType": "DRIVER_LICENSE",
  "rejectedDocumentId": "doc123"
}

Response 201:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Document resubmitted successfully",
  "document": { ... }
}

Errors:
- 400: Invalid request
- 404: Original document not found
- 409: Cannot resubmit non-rejected document
```

---

### Verification Status

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Purpose |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| GET | `/users/:userId/verification-status` | User/Admin | Get user verification status |
| GET | `/users/me/verification-status` | User | Get current user verification status |

**GET /users/me/verification-status**
```json
Response 200:
{
  "userId": "user123",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "emailVerified": true,
  "emailVerifiedAt": "2026-07-01T10:00:00Z",
  "phoneVerified": true,
  "phoneVerifiedAt": "2026-07-02T10:00:00Z",
  "kycVerified": false,
  "kycVerifiedAt": null,
  "verificationStatus": "PHONE_VERIFIED",
  "requirements": {
    "emailRequired": true,
    "phoneRequired": false,
    "kycRequired": false,
    "nextUnlockedFeature": "high_value_transactions"
  }
}
```

---

### Admin KYC Management

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Purpose |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| GET | `/admin/kyc/pending` | Admin | List pending KYC verifications |
| POST | `/admin/kyc/:userId/approve` | Admin | Approve KYC for user |
| POST | `/admin/kyc/:userId/reject` | Admin | Reject KYC with reason |
| GET | `/admin/kyc/user/:userId/history` | Admin | View verification history |

**GET /admin/kyc/pending?limit=20&offset=0**
```json
Response 200:
{
  "total": 45,
  "pending": [
    {
      "id": "doc123",
      "userId": "user456",
      "userEmail": "seller@example.com",
      "documentType": "PASSPORT",
      "uploadedAt": "2026-07-05T14:30:00Z",
      "status": "PENDING"
    }
  ]
}
```

**POST /admin/kyc/:userId/approve**
```json
Response 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "KYC approved",
  "user": {
    "id": "user123",
    "kycVerified": true,
    "kycVerifiedAt": "2026-07-05T15:00:00Z",
    "verificationStatus": "FULLY_VERIFIED"
  }
}
```

**POST /admin/kyc/:userId/reject**
```json
Request:
{
  "rejectionReason": "Document is blurry and unreadable"
}

Response 200:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "KYC rejected",
  "document": {
    "id": "doc123",
    "status": "REJECTED",
    "rejectionReason": "Document is blurry and unreadable"
  }
}
```

